{
  "id": 22,
  "name": "cluster_density_chain",
  "intent": "Anchors on nearest-neighbor (-distance) but boosts candidates with high cluster_density, which measures the fraction of other unvisited cities within mean distance. This steers the tour to complete dense geographic regions before making long jumps to isolated nodes. The bounded cluster bonus (0.35) shifts ranking toward candidates that enable cheap follow-on moves, while the nearest_remaining penalty (-0.15) discourages stranding candidates whose own neighborhoods are sparse (no close unvisited peers). Net effect: prefer dense-cluster interiors over peripheries, leaving the fixed 24-delta 2-opt budget to repair any residual inefficiencies.",
  "tags": [
    "cluster",
    "lookahead"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    nr = f['nearest_remaining']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    return -1.0 * d + 0.35 * cd - 0.15 * nr\n",
